%description:

Tcp.tlpEnabled:off -- only the timer sends the lost last segment again.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "Tail Loss Probe (RFC 8985 section 7): about two SRTTs after the last
transmission or ACK of new data, send one probe, so that its ACK starts the repair of a lost
tail before the RTO".

The classes: on (true, the default, the value of LinuxTcp) and off (false, the value of
LegacyTcp). The code: after each transmission of new data, TcpAlgorithmBase arms the probe
timer of RFC 8985 section 7 (about two SRTTs), and its expiry sends new data or the last
segment again. The probe needs SACK; without SACK, the class is the same as off. This test separates "off" from "on".

Host under test: host1, which sends three segments; the round trip is 40 ms, and the tap drops the third segment
once. Nothing follows it, so no SACK can show the loss. Observation: level 1, no transmission of the third segment in 0.8 s after the first one; the
timer retransmits it about 1 s after the ACK of the first two segments.

%# parameter: Tcp.tlpEnabled
%# class: off
%# value: false
%# key: *.host1.tcp.tlpEnabled
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpTlpEnabledOff")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 2896 && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B").nth(1).drop()
                     .describe("the third data segment of host1, the first time"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 2896 && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
             .describe("the third data segment of host1")
             .within(2.0))
        .never(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
              .filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 2896 && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
              .describe("an early retransmission of the third segment, by the timer")
              .within(0.8))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 2896 && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
             .describe("retransmission of the third segment, by the timer")
             .within(0.7));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpTlpEnabledOff compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.tlpEnabled = false    # the parameter under test
*.linkDelay = 10ms
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 4344B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpTlpEnabledOff: PASS
